    <data name="Faq1Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>When can I get the app?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq1Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>On {0}, from 8:00, for iPhone, Android and the web. On iPhone you can pre-order it now, and it downloads by itself that morning.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq2Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Will it cost anything?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq2Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>No. The app is free, and so is the first coffee for everyone on the waitlist. Prices in the app are the same as at the counter.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq3Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What happens to my paper stamp card?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq3Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Bring it to any of our cafés from {0} and we'll move its stamps into the app. Paper cards keep working until {1}.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq4Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Can I order for a group?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq4Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Yes, up to eight drinks in one order. For something bigger, like an office breakfast, email us a day ahead.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq5Question" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>What do you do with my email?</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Faq5Answer" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>We send one email on launch day, and product news only if you ticked the box. Every email has a link to leave the list.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>About Little Copper</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutHeadingStart" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Three cafés, and a machine called</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutHeadingEm" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Little Copper</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutDescription" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>How a copper lever espresso machine from 1961 gave three Copenhagen cafés their name, the people behind them, and their opening hours.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutLede" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Ida Mørch and Omar Haddad opened the first café on Elmegade in Nørrebro in 2016, around a copper lever machine from 1961 that Ida's grandfather had kept in his garage.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="MachineAlt" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The copper lever espresso machine from 1961 on the counter in Nørrebro</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>From one counter to three</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody1" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The machine needed six months of repairs and still wants a gentle hand. It pulls about 400 coffees on a busy Saturday, and every new barista learns on it first.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="StoryBody2" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Vesterbro followed in 2019, with a kitchen for brunch, and Christianshavn in 2022, small enough to know every regular by name. The queues grew with them, and that's why we're building the app.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="AboutCafesTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Our three cafés</value>
    </data>
    <data name="TeamTitle" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>The people behind the counter</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team1Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Ida Mørch</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team1Role" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Co-founder, roasts the coffee</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team1Note" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Roasts twice a week in a shed in Valby, and still repairs the machine herself.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team2Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Omar Haddad</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team2Role" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Co-founder, runs the cafés</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team2Note" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Opens Nørrebro at seven most mornings and knows the regulars' orders before they do.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team3Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Nanami Sato</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team3Role" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Head barista</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team3Note" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Trains every new barista on the 1961 machine.</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team4Name" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Lukas Berg</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team4Role" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Builds the app</value>
    </data>
    <data name="Team4Note" xml:space="preserve">
        <value>Timed the morning queue for a month before writing a line of code.</value>
    </data>
